sts whose research, teaching, and engagement contribute to inclusive and intellectually vibrant academic communities. Through sustained mentorship, professional development, and full participation in the intellectual life of the College, fellows are supported as they … Continue reading \"2027 Gaius Charles Bolin Dissertation and Post-MFA Fellowship: Statistics\" more » Anthropology and Sociology Department: Tenure-Track Cultural Anthropologist Description The Williams College Department of Anthropology and Sociology invites applications for a tenure-track sociocultural anthropologist whose expertise would complement those of the current faculty. The department has a unique interdisciplinary focus that emphasizes innovative, empirically grounded qualitative work, including ethnography, historical comparative anthropology and sociology, visual methods, and other qualitative traditions. For this position … Continue reading \"Anthropology and Sociology Department: Tenure-Track Cultural Anthropologist\" more » Chemistry Department Description The Williams College Chemistry Department invites applications for a two-year visiting assistant professor position and for a one-year visiting assistant professor position, both beginning in July 2026, in any subspecialty. We especially seek candidates who can contribute to the intellectual vibrancy and diversity of the academic community through their research, teaching and service, and who will … Continue reading \"Chemistry Department\" more » Department of Asian Languages, Literatures, and Cultures Description Applications are invited for a one-year visiting position in Japanese language for 2026-27, with teaching to begin in September 2026. Depending on the candidate’s qualifications, the appointment will be made at the level of either a visiting lecturer or a visiting assistant professor. The teaching load will consist of four language courses in 2026-2027.Depending … Continue reading \"Department of Asian Languages, Literatures, and Cultures\" more » Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education Description Williams College invites applications for the position of Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education, a faculty role within the Department of  Physical Education, Athletics, and Recreation. The College is seeking a candidate who can recruit and coach a talented, motivated, diverse and hardworking team of student-athletes who will individually and … Continue reading \"Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Head Women’s Lacrosse Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education\" more » Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Head Wrestling Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education Description Williams College invites applications for the position of Head Wrestling Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education, a faculty role within the Department of Physical Education, Athletics, and Recreation. The College is seeking a candidate who can recruit and coach a talented, motivated, diverse and hardworking team of student-athletes who will individually and collectively … Continue reading \"Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Head Wrestling Coach and Assistant Professor of Physical Education\" more » Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sport Supervision and Compliance Description In this role, the successful candidate will provide high-level mentorship to a group of coaches at all stages of their careers, meeting with these coaches regularly and attending practices and competitions to gain insight and provide meaningful feedback. The position will be responsible for spearheading the search process and onboarding of new head coaches … Continue reading \"Department of Athletics and Physical Education: Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sport Supervision and Compliance\" more » Department of Music Description The Department of Music at Williams College announces a fixed-term renewable, half-time (.5 FTE) position of Lyell B. Clay Artist in Residence in Piano, to begin fall of 2026. The initial contract is for 3 years and is renewable thereafter on an ongoing basis. This is a benefits-eligible position; details can be found here … Continue reading \"Department of Music\" more » Department of Music Description The Department of Music at Williams College announces a one-year, full-time Visiting Assistant Professor appointment in Musicology beginning in the fall of 2026. DUTIES: Teach four courses (two per semester), including a survey of European music history up to 1750 primarily for majors, introductory courses on early music, and other courses related to the … Continue reading \"Department of Music\" more » Economics Department Description The Williams College Economics Department invites applications for two tenure-track positions in applied microeconomics, to begin July 1, 2026. We are particularly seeking candidates whose work relates to applied microeconomic theory, development economics, economics of education, gender economics, health economics, household behavior and family economics, industrial organization, labor economics, public economics, public policy, political … Continue reading \"Economics Department\" more » English Department Description The English Department at Williams College invites applications for a tenure-track position in African American Literature at the level of Assistant Professor, to begin Fall 2026. We particularly welcome candidates whose interests include the relation of African American literature to global Black anglophone literature. Other interests might include gender and sexuality studies, environmental criticism, … Continue reading \"English Department\" more » English Department: Assistant Professor in British or Anglophone Literature 1800-1950 Description The English Department at Williams College invites applications for a tenure-track position in British or Anglophone Literature, 1800-1950, at the level of Assistant Professor, to begin Fall 2027. We welcome applicants who work in any area of British or Anglophone literature and culture in this period.  Additional interests include film and / or media … Continue reading \"English Department: Assistant Professor in British or Anglophone Literature 1800-1950\" more » Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Department: Open Rank Professor in Gender and Sexuality Studies of the Global South Description Open Rank Professor in Gender and Sexuality Studies of the Global South in the Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Program at Williams College The program in Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies (WGSS) seeks a professor who does research on gender and sexuality from countries or regions in the Global South. We are seeking candidates … Continue reading \"Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Department: Open Rank Professor in Gender and Sexuality Studies of the Global South\" more » Section Menu Employment MENU Employment Faculty Open Positions Graduate Fellowships Onboarding Resources Faculty Resource Site Staff Staff Careers New Hire Resources Students Academic Year Employment​ Handshake​ Supervisors Resources Parents & Families Our Community Welcome! Visitor Guide Berkshires.org Williams College Fast Facts Living Here College Employment Policies Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Workplace Conduct Background Check Policy​ Employment Laws​​ Faculty and Staff Handbooks Annual Security Report​ Spouse Partner Resources Affiliated Offices Human Resources Dean of the Faculty Institutional Diversity and Equity Employment Williamstown, MA 01267 USA Visit Campus Map Land Acknowledgment Directory Employment Accessibility Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Comment Form Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Log In · Copyright 2026 wp-web5.williams.edu Facebook logo Instagram logo LinkedIn logo Threads logo X logo YouTube logo"
