    "https://employment.williams.edu/staff/": {
      "title": "Staff",
      "description": "Staff – Employment Skip to main content Go to Williams College Home Menu & Search use tab and shift-tab to navigate once expanded Search Williams Search Box Search Suggestions Type in your search terms and press enter or navigate down for suggested search results. About Overview Mission Fast Facts Governance Academics Areas of Study Course Catalog Academic Calendar Tutorials Graduate Programs Study Away Winter Study Libraries Experiential Learning & Community Engagement Pathways for Inclusive Excellence Admission & Aid Apply Affordability Financial Aid Tours Life at Williams Overview Bookstore Dining Housing Health Services Integrative Wellbeing Services Religion & Spirituality Students ▶ Alumni ▶ Parents & Families ▶ Employment ▶ Faculty & Staff ▶ Apply Visit Give Quick Links: Arts Athletics Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Campus Map Directory Events News & Stories Williams Email Employment Staff Thank you for your interest in employment opportunities at Williams College. Williams is a special place to work and grow in a career, rich in opportunity, experiences, and rewards. Beyond fully meeting its legal obligations for non-discrimination, Williams College is committed to building a diverse and inclusive community where members from all backgrounds can live, learn, and thrive. Career Opportunities Browse and search open positions on the Williams Staff Careers page, and create an account to apply. How to Apply Our careers site is new. Please read on to learn more about how to set up an account and apply. External Applicants Create An Account Select the Sign In option at the top right corner of your screen. If this is your first time visiting, select Create Account at the bottom of the pop-up window. It will prompt you to enter a username and a unique password. Once you have created your account and verified your email address, you will be able to sign in. Click to copy link Browse Postings You can scroll through the list of available jobs, or you can use the search bar and filters underneath the purple Williams banner to narrow your search. Available filters include: Full or Part Time Job Category Faculty, Staff, or Temporary More Contractor Fixed Term Regular Each individual job posting includes a title, location, time type, date the job was posted, and the official Job Requisition (JR) number. If you have questions about a job, you can email hr​@williams​.edu and ask about the JR number. Once you find a job that interests you, select the job title to open the job description and minimum requirements. The expanded details will include whether the job is fully onsite, hybrid, or fully remote, a full job description, minimum requirements, and preferred qualifications. Click to copy link Apply For A Job Select a job posting title to open the expanded detail view on the right side of your screen. At the very top, under the title, there is a purple Apply button. A pop-up window will open. You can: Autofill with Resume: upload your resume and let Workday copy it into the application. Apply Manually: fill out the application yourself. Use My Last Application: If you have already applied for a job at Williams, copy your last application to this one. Please complete the application in its entirety. If you auto-filled your information, please double-check and ensure that everything is accurate before submitting your application. Click to copy link Track Your Application Select the Candidate Home tab in the top right corner of your screen. My Tasks will be blank. Underneath My Tasks, there is a section called My Applications. Here, you can track the status of your applications. “Your application has been received”- indicates that you have successfully submitted your application. “Application in progress”- indicates that your application is under review. “Not selected” - indicates that you have not been selected to move forward for that particular position. Please note that applicants will receive email notifications and status updates to their Workday account. Click to copy link Internal Applicants Log into Workday and apply through the jobs hub. When Will I Hear Back? Job openings are usually posted for several weeks, after which the Search Committee begins its review and selects the candidates who will be invited to the phone interview stage. Due to the volume of applications, applicants who are not selected to move forward may not be notified until the search is completed. It is not unusual for this entire process to take multiple months. We know it can seem like forever, but trust that we value your application and will be in touch as soon as possible! If you have any questions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at HR​@Williams​.edu or 413.597.2681. If you require an accommodation to complete the application or interview process, please notify us in advance so we can make the necessary arrangements. Follow Us on LinkedIn Print this page Section Menu Employment MENU Employment Faculty Open Positions Graduate Fellowships Onboarding Resources Faculty Resource Site Staff Staff Careers New Hire Resources Students Academic Year Employment​ Handshake​ Supervisors Resources Parents & Families Our Community Welcome! Visitor Guide Berkshires.org Williams College Fast Facts Living Here College Employment Policies Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Workplace Conduct Background Check Policy​ Employment Laws​​ Faculty and Staff Handbooks Annual Security Report​ Spouse Partner Resources Affiliated Offices Human Resources Dean of the Faculty Institutional Diversity and Equity Employment Williamstown, MA 01267 USA Visit Campus Map Land Acknowledgment Directory Employment Accessibility Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Comment Form Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Log In · Copyright 2026 wp-web5.williams.edu Facebook logo Instagram logo LinkedIn logo Threads logo X logo YouTube logo"
    }
